  "id": "CR-02",
  "name": "Demand spike",
  "description": "Demand across the Dhaka region jumps to 1.8x for 8 hours, starting 1 hour after the reset. The platform must flag the scheduled event, raise the stockout risk for Dhaka stations and ship ahead of the stockouts. The spike is announced by a simulator event and the forecaster reads each station's live demand multiplier, so it is explained demand: the residual-based demand_anomaly detector (unexplained demand, tests/test_backend_units.py) correctly stays quiet.\n",
